menuconfig ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG
    bool "Runtime-configurable rotary encoder (torabo-tsuki)"
    help
      Per-layer assignments for a rotary encoder — clockwise, counter-clockwise
      and the push button — editable live over BLE from Torabo-Studio.

      The encoder is not a keymap key: rotation rides ZMK's sensor path and the
      button rides the input path, and both resolve what to fire from this store.
      That is why an encoder needs no matrix transform, no physical-layout entry
      and no keymap edits.

      Default n; enable per build target (see the torabo-encoder-live snippet).

if ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG

config ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG_BLE
    bool "Expose the encoder settings over a BLE GATT service"
    depends on BT
    default y
    help
      Encrypted GATT service e1f4ad00 to read/write the assignments live. The
      config is ~124 B, so it fits in a single ATT write and needs no Write Long.

config ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG_TUNNEL
    bool "Expose the encoder settings over the Studio RPC torabo tunnel"
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO_TORABO_TUNNEL
    default y
    help
      Register the settings with the torabo tunnel so they are reachable over
      whichever transport Studio RPC is using (USB serial included).
      Carries the exact same wire blob as the GATT service (feature id 0x0D), and
      coexists with it.

module = ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG
module-str = ZMK Encoder Config
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ZMK_ENCODER_CONFIG
